# Waiting on our own model

Anything the product understands from **user text or a user upload** must eventually be decided by our own structuring model, reached only through the Platform BFF. The UI never calls an AI provider. Anthropic is a temporary stand-in, not a target.

Whenever the UI (or the local bridge) decides something that model will decide — which app a message or file belongs to, what a file contains, what to say back, what to suggest next — mark it:

```
// WAITING MODEL: <what our structuring model should decide>
```

Use that exact token (`WAITING MODEL`) so a later grep finds every site.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — reads as real logic, invisible when the model lands
if (/boxout|door/i.test(stem)) return "boxouts";

// ✅ GOOD
// WAITING MODEL: the model picks the app from inspector facts, not the file name
if (/boxout|door/i.test(stem)) return "boxouts";
```

- A hand-written heuristic counts as a model stand-in even though no model runs: keyword matching, format-to-app tables and canned replies are exactly what the token is for.
- Deterministic facts (extension, MIME type, size, object counts) belong to the BFF file inspector, not the model. Do not tag pure format detection.
- Keep the note to one line: what is faked and what our model decides instead.

## Which token

| Token | Swap it marks |
| --- | --- |
| `WAITING MODEL` | the brain: who decides (Anthropic or a heuristic today, our structuring model later) |
| `WAITING BFF` | the transport: who we call and in what shape |
| `WAITING DATABASE` | the store: where state lives |

They are separate axes. A site that needs two swaps carries both tokens, one per line. Do not invent a fourth marker.

Full contracts, the swap table and the cutover checklist live in [docs/model-integration.md](../../docs/model-integration.md). Read it before changing how chat or file intake behaves.
